Spring boot project
config directory where the config.yml file is to run the kind cluster with 1 worker node
vprofile project
git clone-->mvn test-->mvn build-->codescanner-->repository-->kubernetescluster deploy

appimage: vprofile/vprofileapp:V1
	runs on port 8080
	
dbimage: vprofile/vprofiledb:V1
	in application.properties file
	host: vprodb
	password: vprodbpass

	this image had intially created accounts database already 
	mysql -u root -pvprodbpass

using the kubernetes for the deployment
	kind cluster is used
	apiVersion: kind.x-k8s.io/v1alpha4

applications.properties file
#JDBC Configutation for Database Connection
jdbc.driverClassName=com.mysql.jdbc.Driver
jdbc.url=jdbc:mysql://vprodb:3306/accounts?useUnicode=true&characterEncoding=UTF-8&zeroDateTimeBehavior=convertToNull
jdbc.username=root
jdbc.password=vprodbpass

#Memcached Configuration For Active and StandBy Host
#For Active Host
memcached.active.host=vprocache01
memcached.active.port=11211
#For StandBy Host
memcached.standBy.host=vprocache02
memcached.standBy.port=11211

#RabbitMq Configuration
rabbitmq.address=vpromq01
rabbitmq.port=15672
rabbitmq.username=guest
rabbitmq.password=guest


for the memcached and rabbitmq we used the offical direct images and assigned there env values , host , port numbers to it
images
memcached
rabbitmq

NOTE: in service file at metadata the name is the name of the host address or host name that is the name service runs

      jdbc.password and rabbitmq.password both are kept into the secret.yml file with type opaque
      rabbitmq.username is kept into the configmap file 

added the volumes to db deployment

if we create the volume like below the data directory will be created in the wokernode i,e in kind cluster the worker node
is the container

        volumeMounts:
          - mountPath: /var/lib/mysql
            name: dbvol
      volumes:
        - name: dbvol
          hostPath:
            path: /data
            type: DirectoryOrCreate


we need to get into the container to see the data directory and the data in it

docker exec -it 1ca976d0dfa8 /bin/bash

1ca976d0dfa8 -- worker node id


Created the Persistent volume and persentent volume claim
hostPath: /opt/mysql-data

get into the node or docker container node for kind cluster then go to /opt/mysql-data



